{
  "_note": "Sector labels come from the publication. One article belongs to exactly one sector - a feed listed twice would manufacture fake cross-sector spread. GDELT was removed: it now returns 429 on every run from shared CI addresses, and the articles it did supply are backdated imports rather than live observations. The adapter remains in collect.py for a manual backfill. Feeds carry a country because geography must come from provenance, not from what an article mentions: a US publication writing about China is US coverage. Every feed here has answered a probe. A feed may carry a sector label only if its whole beat sits in that sector: a general business publication cannot, because its articles about other industries would be counted as this one and would manufacture cross-sector spread that never happened. That test is about the beat, not the country - foreign trade press with a narrow beat belongs in the main pipeline exactly as domestic trade press does.",
